    Thanks <a
    href="https://github.com/trevor-scheer"><code>@​trevor-scheer</code></a>!
    - Redesign GraphiQL with light and dark themes, an endpoint and Run bar,
    a plugin activity rail, a resizable side panel, a status bar, and a
    Variables/Headers tab strip. The Documentation Explorer, History, and
    Monaco editor themes follow the same design. Settings offer theme,
    density, and font-size controls.</p>
    <p>The top bar joins Run/Stop with the selected operation name, its
    QRY/MUT/SUB label, and an HTTP method selector. Selecting an operation
    does not execute it; use Run or the keyboard shortcut. The method menu
    offers Auto for queries and explains unavailable options. Selected rows
    use the GraphQL logo pink, while keyboard focus has a separate
    outline.</p>
    <p>The response pane adds HTTP method, status, timing, and size from
    transports that provide them, a copy action, and persisted JSON, Tree,
    and Table views. Tree expands response objects and arrays; Table
    presents each list field separately. Saved operations show when they
    have unsaved edits, and tabs with multiple operations identify the
    active operation.</p>
    <p>Improve keyboard focus visibility and screen-reader labels throughout
    the interface. Escape cancels History label edits and returns focus to
    the edit button. Closing Settings returns focus to its trigger.</p>
    <p>Unify GraphQL syntax coloring across Documentation Explorer, History,
    and Query Builder. Use the <code>--type-scalar</code>,
    <code>--type-enum</code>, <code>--type-input</code>, and
    <code>--type-composite</code> CSS tokens and the exported
    <code>typeCategory</code> helper to customize type-category colors.</p>
    <p>The design tokens use OKLCH colors, and the build targets the
    <code>defaults</code> browserslist preset. The v5 <code>--color-*</code>
    variables remain defined but no longer theme the built-in UI; migrate
    existing overrides to the new OKLCH tokens. Custom CSS that overrides
    internal class names may also need updating. See <a
    href="https://github.com/graphql/graphiql/blob/c2e792bc446d5d6751bd7cd1d9ac283a4a1d8fc4/docs/migration/graphiql-6.0.0.md#css-and-retheming">CSS
    and retheming</a> for migration guidance. Refs <a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/graphql/graphiql/issues/4219">graphql/graphiql#4219</a>.</p>
    </li>
